Z||000016||stsmithgt||12-08-1999||12:40 PM||||A small story.  I was 16 working on the same crew as my dad in Louisiana putting in natural gas lines.  The boss told me to go get his truck down the road one day.  I looked at my dad because I had never driven with a clutch before.  My dad gave me the advise,"Go get it." gee thanks dad.  Turned out to be no big deal.  Luckily it was parked in the dirt for first gear. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>A dirt road or a nice empty oil slicked parking lot is always fun especialy after a rain to practice with that clutch. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Well if a gear gets banged accidently, I'd rather have my tires spin then the drivetrain to absorb the impact.  High speeds on public roads aren't neccesary to learn clutch use.  ||||reg||1
